### JobMaster API — run these from IntelliJ's HTTP client (or copy as curl).
### Start the app first: ./gradlew bootRun
### (add --args='--spring.profiles.active=mock' to test without spending credits)

### Health — shows active AI provider/model and whether a profile exists
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Get stored profile
GET http://localhost:8080/api/profile

### Store/update the master profile (fill in your own data — or use the Profile tab).
### This is the single source of truth the AI tailors from — keep it current.
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Max Mustermann",
  "email": "max.mustermann@example.com",
  "phone": "+49 170 0000000",
  "location": "Berlin, Germany",
  "links": {
    "LinkedIn": "https://linkedin.com/in/example"
  },
  "headline": "Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Backend engineer building Java microservices and REST APIs.",
  "skills": {
    "Languages": ["Java", "Python"],
    "Frameworks": ["Spring Boot", "React"],
    "Tools": ["Docker", "PostgreSQL", "AWS"]
  },
  "experiences": [
    {
      "company": "Example Tech GmbH",
      "title": "Software Engineer",
      "team": null,
      "location": "Berlin, Germany",
      "startDate": "Jan 2023",
      "endDate": "Present",
      "bullets": [
        "Built Spring Boot microservices serving 10,000 daily users.",
        "Cut API response times by 40% through query optimization."
      ],
      "technologies": ["Java", "Spring Boot", "PostgreSQL"]
    }
  ],
  "education": [
    {
      "institution": "Technische Universität Berlin",
      "degree": "M.Sc. Computer Science",
      "location": "Berlin, Germany",
      "startDate": "Oct 2020",
      "endDate": "Sep 2022",
      "highlights": []
    }
  ],
  "projects": [],
  "certifications": [],
  "languages": ["English (C1)", "German (B1)"]
}

### Tailor CV to a job description (one-page output).
### location: overrides the profile location on this document only.
### applicationId: attach to a board application; omit to auto-create one.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/cv
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobTitle": "Backend Engineer",
  "company": "TechCo",
  "location": "Berlin, Germany",
  "jobDescription": "Paste the full job description here...",
  "extraInstructions": ""
}

### Generate a cover letter (cvGenerationId = id returned by POST /api/cv;
### the letter then attaches to the same application as that CV)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/cover-letter
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobTitle": "Backend Engineer",
  "company": "TechCo",
  "location": "Berlin, Germany",
  "jobDescription": "Paste the full job description here...",
  "tone": "professional",
  "cvGenerationId": 1
}

### List all generations (newest first) — your per-job application history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/generations

### Get one generation with full content
GET http://localhost:8080/api/generations/1

### Download a generation as a one-page PDF (works for CV and cover letter)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/generations/1/pdf

### ---------- Application tracker (the Kanban board) ----------

### Add a job to the board (status starts as SAVED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobTitle": "Backend Engineer",
  "company": "TechCo",
  "location": "Berlin, Germany",
  "jobDescription": "Paste the job description here...",
  "jobUrl": "https://example.com/jobs/123",
  "salary": "70-80k €",
  "contactPerson": "Jane Doe",
  "notes": "referred by Alex"
}

### List all applications with their documents
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications

### Get one application
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1

### Update any subset of fields; moving status to APPLIED sets appliedAt automatically.
### Statuses: SAVED | APPLIED | INTERVIEWING | OFFER | REJECTED
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "APPLIED",
  "notes": "sent via portal"
}

### Delete an application (also deletes its generated documents)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1

### Token & cost usage report (totals + per-month + per-model)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/usage

### ---------- Job watcher ----------

### Watched companies (SAP, Delivery Hero, EGYM seeded on first start)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/watch/companies

### Watch a new company (adapter configs:
###   SMARTRECRUITERS {"companyId": "..."} | PERSONIO {"host": "acme.jobs.personio.de"}
###   SUCCESSFACTORS {"baseUrl": "...", "listPath": "/go/.../12345/", "maxPages": 10})
POST http://localhost:8080/api/watch/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme",
  "adapterType": "PERSONIO",
  "configJson": "{\"host\": \"acme.jobs.personio.de\"}",
  "includeKeywords": "software|developer|engineer|backend|java",
  "locations": "germany|munich|remote"
}

### Check all enabled companies now
POST http://localhost:8080/api/watch/run

### Recent run log
GET http://localhost:8080/api/watch/runs

### New postings feed (status=NEW | ALL | SEEN | DISMISSED | CONVERTED)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/jobs?status=NEW

### Turn a posting into a board application / dismiss it
POST http://localhost:8080/api/jobs/1/convert
POST http://localhost:8080/api/jobs/1/dismiss
